"el": "Άρνηση, ερώτηση, μόρια",
"title": "Negation, questions and particles",
"span": "A1–B1",
"part": "Μέρος ΣΤ΄ | Σύνταξη | Syntax",
"blurb": "Which \"not\" to use (δεν, μη, όχι), double negatives (δεν είδα τίποτα), ούτε, the question words and tag questions, μήπως and άραγε, and the small particles that give speech its colour: πια, ακόμα, κιόλας, καν, ντε, δα, ρε.",
"intro": [
{
"p": "Greek has three words for \"not\": **δεν** with ordinary verbs, **μη(ν)** after να / ας and in prohibitions, and **όχι** for everything that isn't a verb. Negative words like **τίποτα, κανείς, ποτέ** need a δεν as well: **Δεν είδα τίποτα.** \"I didn't see anything.\" Questions are made with intonation alone: **Θέλεις καφέ;** \"Do you want coffee?\""
},
